  "info": "West coast, twice.\n\nmodular   the parts patched by hand: a modulation osc into the principal osc's pm input (its size from an envelope plus a random value each note), then a wavefolder (opened by a second envelope and a slow random wander), a pluck gate, voices, a plate. Click the nodes and move them about.\nemulator  the same idea in one node, `westcoast`, with its own two envelopes and a `drift` that keeps the fold, fm and pitch wandering. Different ratio and a saw as the principal, so the two lanes do not match.\n\nii V I VI in C (Dm9, G13, Cmaj9, A7b13), twice round. Try: the pluck gate's close (ring-out), the folder's fold, the index envelope's amount, then wave 8 on the principal oscillator and draw your own."
 },
